# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Burhan platform — environment template (copy to .env; NEVER commit .env)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Platform database (P2-D: PostgreSQL) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev : bash scripts/pg_dev_start.sh  (prints a ready URI — unprivileged
#             pgserver cluster on 127.0.0.1:55432; no docker, no root)
# Compose   : docker compose up -d  (postgres:17-alpine, password below)
#
# PRIVILEGE SEPARATION (order items 1.2+2.3, 2026-10-31) — two identities:
#   * MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL (owner) — migrate deploy + role provisioning
#     ONLY (bash scripts/db_app_role.sh provisions the limited role and
#     prints the app URL; run it after EVERY migrate deploy)
#   * DATABASE_URL (the app) — the limited `burhan_app` role: DML only,
#     no TRUNCATE/DDL. The audit trail's trigger cannot block TRUNCATE —
#     the missing privilege is the defense.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://burhan@127.0.0.1:5432/burhan"
BURHAN_APP_DB_PASSWORD="change-me-too-long-random"
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://burhan_app:change-me-too-long-random@127.0.0.1:5432/burhan"

# Only used by docker-compose.yml (POSTGRES container credential):
POSTGRES_PASSWORD="change-me-long-random"

# ── Auth (next-auth 4, src/lib/auth.ts) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="change-me-openssl-rand-base64-32"
# The public origin as browsers see it (required in production, behind Caddy):
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Engine bridge (src/lib/engine.ts) ────────────────────────────────────────
# All optional; sensible defaults resolve from the repo root.
# BURHAN_PYTHON=python3
# BURHAN_ENGINE_DIR=/srv/sen
# BURHAN_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/sen/saas-data
# Lab mode: allow non-demo scans of private-network targets — default OFF.
# EXACT semantics (order 2.8, 2026-10-31): the ONLY value that enables lab
# mode is the exact string "1" — every other value ("0", "false", "true",
# "yes", unset, empty) leaves it OFF (src/lib/engine.ts labModeEnabled).
# When OFF: private/link-local/metadata/CGNAT targets are rejected at target
# creation AND at PATCH, and the engine re-validates every connection (incl.
# DNS answers and redirect hops) and fails closed. The demo target is the
# only private egress by construction (it is the platform's own fixture).
# Current deployments: unset (safe default) — docker-compose, Caddyfile and
# every start script leave it unset.
# BURHAN_ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS=0
